[WARNING & FORWARD COMPATIBILITY ASSUMPTION NOTICE]
================================================================================
WARNING:
PlannedEducation sets lowest probable limit requirements (using `>=` or `^`)
rather than hard-pinned exact versions (`==`). This design ensures the platform
can readily accept critical upstream security patches and newer minor/patch releases.

COMPATIBILITY ASSUMPTION:
We assume forward compatibility with newer releases beyond the lowest minimum.
However, because major or breaking changes in cutting-edge external libraries
can occasionally introduce subtle regressions:
1. All core functionality, deterministic grading, proctoring, and visual interfaces
   have been verified against the exact "Tested Working Version" column below.
2. If you install unpinned packages and observe runtime crashes, unexpected
   Pydantic validation errors, or build failures, DOWNGRADE the affected package
   to the exact "Tested Working Version" documented in the matrix below.

DOWNGRADE COMMAND EXAMPLES:
  Python: pip install "<package_name>==<tested_version>"
  Node:   npm install "<package_name>@<tested_version>"

